    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16198" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσιγμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without sigma,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾠδαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Comp.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ᾠδή,</span> name of a poem
			of <i><span class="en">
				Lasus
			</span></i>
			<i>without a sigma in it,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				10.455c
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσιγμοποιέω</span></b> , <i>compose such a poem,</i>
		ibid.</div>
